se at all. ?]
view-if: popular_front_coalition_heartland >= 50 and not concord_formed
choose-if: (((collectivist_relation >= 65 and collectivist_leader == "Halsmark") or (collectivist_relation >= 45 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators")) and ((unionist_relation >= 45 and unionist_leader == "Joos") or (unionist_relation >= 40 and unionist_leader == "Emperor") or (unionist_relation >= 65 and unionist_ideology == "Right" and collectivist_leader != "Conciliators") or (unionist_relation >= 55 and unionist_ideology == "Right" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators")) and ((liberal_parliament = 1 or lvp_formed) or ((ddp_relation >= 50 and ddp_ideology != "Left") or (ddp_relation >= 40 and ddp_ideology == "Left"))) and communist_coalition >= 3) or (unionist_leader == "Joos" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and unionist_relation >= 35 and collectivist_relation >= 35) or (unionist_leader == "Emperor" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and unionist_relation >= 30 and collectivist_relation >= 30)

Could we really form a coalition that included both the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span>? It seems like an absurd concept, but given our good relationships with both sides, it is not an impossibility.

[? if president == "DuFour": DuFour might object to this, and may perform a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> on our government, if such a coalition is formed.?]

- @popular_front_2: Form the Popular Front!
- @great_popular_front: Form the Popular Front!

@popular_front_2
view-if: unionist_ideology != "Left" or collectivist_leader != "Conciliators"

Somehow, both the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] are at the very least willing to entertain negotiations. Of course, <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> radicals and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] conservatives derail the negotiations almost immediately. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> demands leadership of the coalition for themselves, [? if marcher_r_heartland > collectivist_r_heartland : despite our higher vote share, ?]while the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is offended by the prospect of helping <span style="color: #700000;">**Bolsheviks**</span> enter government. Memories of the <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> against similar governments in Stathmore and Dornwich remain vivid, standing as a cautionary tale.

*Something* must be done to restore balance.

- @popular_front_resources
- @popular_front_democracy
- @popular_front_braun
- @coalition_menu: This is impossible. Try another governing arrangement.

@popular_front_resources
title: Use our resources to smooth things over.
unavailable-subtitle: Required: 3 resources
subtitle: -3 resources
choose-if: resources >= 3
on-arrival: resources -= 3
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_democracy
title: Convince the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> to accept democracy.
subtitle: [? if collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" : The Conciliator leadership of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> at least claim to support the Popular Front. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: Our relationship with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is not high enough.
choose-if: (collectivist_relation >= 60 and communist_coalition >= 3) or collectivist_leader == "Conciliators"
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_braun
title: Use pressure from President [+ president +] to force the parties to cooperate.
view-if: president_ideology == "Left"
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_success
on-arrival: in_popular_front_heartland = 1; heartland_leader = "Pendrigon"; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 1.5 if liberal_parliament = 0; lvp_right += 3; liberal_cooperation += 3 if liberal_parliament = 1; liberal_cooperation += 2 if (liberal_parliament = 1 and in_popular_front or in_left_front); bourgeois_cooperation += 3; bourgeois_cooperation += 2 if in_popular_front or in_left_front; gold_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 5; collectivist_relation += 8; ddp_relation -= 5 if liberal_parliament = 1; coup_progress += 1; coup_progress += 1 if in_popular_front; reformist_dissent += 20; reformist_strength -= 10; left_dissent -= 10; left_strength += 10; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 1 if liberal_parliament = 0; vanguard_strength += 50; vanguard_militancy += 0.05; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.1; marcher_heartland = 1
go-to: kpd_goals_prussia

Somehow, surprisingly, the coalition is successfully formed! We still need a Minister-President; the only acceptable choice among the parties was [? if left_split == 1:&nbsp;<span style="color: #9B0000;">**SAPD**</span> member?] Emrys Pendrigon, who [? if left_split == 0: belongs?][? if left_split == 1: belonged?] to the left faction of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and had a history of defending <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> members through his work. He is accepted with great reluctance to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and welcomed by the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

In response to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s entrance into the government, the right-wing takes a "wait-and-see" approach for now. They expect that the Popular Front government will be unstable and incompetent, and will collapse of its own accord, discrediting the left and center and eventually enabling the destruction of the Unity Republic. Our task is to prove them wrong. [? if in_left_front: The right will be more active in resisting our rule considering we are also ruling with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> on the federal level too. ?]

@great_popular_front
view-if: unionist_ideology == "Left" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators"
on-arrival: collectivist_relation += 5; unionist_relation += 5; ddp_relation += 5 if (liberal_parliament == 0 and not lvp_formed)
go-to: popular_front_success

Somehow, the coalition is successfully formed! The conciliatory leadership of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> helped make the negotiations possible. We still need a Minister-President; the only acceptable choice among the parties was[? if left_split == 1:&nbsp;<span style="color: #9B0000;">**SAPD**</span> member?] Emrys Pendrigon, who [? if left_split == 0: belongs?][? if left_split == 1: belonged?] to the left faction of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and had a history of defending <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> members through his work. He is accepted with great reluctance to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and welcomed by the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

@kpd_goals_prussia
on-arrival: collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 1; interior_goal_heartland = 0; bureaucracy_goal_heartland = 1; bureaucracy_goal_seen_heartland = 1; free_collectivist_goal_heartland = 1; free_collectivist_goal_seen_heartland = 1; vanguard_goal_heartland = 0; interior_goal_heartland = 1 if (loyalist_banned == 0 or warden_banned == 0); interior_goal_heartland = 2 if (loyalist_banned == 0 and warden_banned == 0); interior_goal_seen_heartland = 1 if (loyalist_banned == 0 or warden_banned == 0); vanguard_goal_heartland = 1 if vanguard_banned == 1; vanguard_goal_seen_heartland = 1 if vanguard_banned == 1; collectivist_ultimatum_heartland_timer = 24

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> presents us with a list of demands for the Heartland coalition:

[? if interior_goal_heartland >= 1 : - Ban the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>. ?]

[? if vanguard_goal_heartland = 1 : - Unban the <span style="color: #700000;">**RFB**</span>. ?]

[? if bureaucracy_goal_heartland = 1 : - Purge the bureaucracy. ?]

[? if free_collectivist_goal_heartland = 1 : - Protect <span style="color: #700000;">communist</span> demonstrations. ?]

They say that they expect to see these goals fulfilled in [+ collectivist_ultimatum_heartland_timer +] months. Otherwise, they will vote to dissolve the coalition.

@right_coalition_prussia
title: A Bürgerblock is formed.
subtitle: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + [? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed:<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] + <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> + **Others** ([+ right_coalition_heartland +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color: #000000;">[+ unionist_party_name +]</span>[? if gold_exist and not lvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?][? if lvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?] + <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span> + Others ([+ right_coalition_heartland +]%) [? if (traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not traditionalist_westarp) or (year = 1929 and month >= 7):- The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span> is not interested in a coalition with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].?]
view-if: right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and not concord_formed
choose-if: (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)
on-arrival: in_right_coalition_heartland = 1; hands_tied_heartland = 0; hands_tied_heartland = 1 if ((ddp_relation < 35 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_relation < 40 and lvp_formed) or weimar_coalition_heartland < 45 or concord_formed); heartland_leader = "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick"; burgher_marcher -= 4; landed_marcher -= 2; gold_right += 1; center_dissent += 10 if hands_tied_heartland; left_dissent += 5 if hands_tied_heartland; labor_dissent += 20 if hands_tied_heartland; reformist_dissent += 20 if hands_tied_heartland; knight_dissent += 10 if hands_tied_heartland; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; lvp_right += 1; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.1; heartland_police_strength -= 10; pro_republic -= 3; ddp_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4; gold_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; hands_tied_heartland = 0

